.TH "HTMLINPUTELEMENT.SETSELECTIONRANGE" "3JS" "October 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLInputElement.setSelectionRange \- HTMLInputElement:
setSelectionRange() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]setSelectionRange()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]HTMLInputElement\f[R] interface sets the start and end positions
of the current text selection in an \f[CR]<input>\f[R] element.
This updates the selection state immediately, though the visual
highlight only appears when the element is focused.
.PP
This method updates the \f[CR]HTMLInputElement.selectionStart\f[R],
\f[CR]HTMLInputElement.selectionEnd\f[R], and
\f[CR]HTMLInputElement.selectionDirection\f[R] properties in one call.
If you wish to select \f[B]all\f[R] text of an input element, you can
use the \f[CR]select()\f[R] method instead.
.PP
The selection of an input element can either be a range of characters or
a caret (if nothing is selected).
Therefore, by setting \f[CR]selectionStart\f[R] and
\f[CR]selectionEnd\f[R] to the same value, you can effectively move the
caret to a specific position in the text field.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
setSelectionRange(selectionStart, selectionEnd)
setSelectionRange(selectionStart, selectionEnd, selectionDirection)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]selectionStart\f[R]
The 0\-based index of the first selected character.
An index greater than the length of the element\(cqs value is treated as
pointing to the end of the value.
See the \f[CR]selectionStart\f[R] property.
.TP
\f[B]selectionEnd\f[R]
The 0\-based index of the character \f[I]after\f[R] the last selected
character.
An index greater than the length of the element\(cqs value is treated as
pointing to the end of the value.
If \f[CR]selectionEnd\f[R] is less than \f[CR]selectionStart\f[R], then
both are treated as the value of \f[CR]selectionEnd\f[R].
See the \f[CR]selectionEnd\f[R] property.
.TP
\f[B]selectionDirection\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string indicating the direction in which the selection is considered
to have been performed.
See the \f[CR]selectionDirection\f[R] property.
Possible values:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\(dqforward\(dq\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\(dqbackward\(dq\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\(dqnone\(dq\f[R] if the direction is unknown or irrelevant.
Default value.
.RE
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]InvalidStateError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the element is not one of the following input types:
\f[CR]password\f[R], \f[CR]search\f[R], \f[CR]tel\f[R], \f[CR]text\f[R],
or \f[CR]url\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Selecting text
Click the button in this example to select the third, fourth, and fifth
characters in the text box (\(lqzil\(rq in the word \(lqMozilla\(rq).
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]input\f[R] type=\(dqtext\(dq id=\(dqtext\-box\(dq size=\(dq20\(dq value=\(dqMozilla\(dq />
<\f[B]button\f[R]>Select text</\f[B]button\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]function\f[R] selectText() {
  \f[B]const\f[R] input = document.getElementById(\(dqtext\-box\(dq);
  input.focus();
  input.setSelectionRange(2, 5);
}

document.querySelector(\(dqbutton\(dq).addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, selectText);
.EE
.SS Result
.SS Moving the caret
Passing the same value for \f[CR]selectionStart\f[R] and
\f[CR]selectionEnd\f[R] moves the caret without selecting any text.
Choose a position and click the button to move the caret there.
Position \f[CR]0\f[R] is before the first character, and position
\f[CR]7\f[R] is after the last one.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]input\f[R] type=\(dqtext\(dq id=\(dqcaret\-box\(dq size=\(dq20\(dq value=\(dqMozilla\(dq />
<\f[B]label\f[R]>
  Position
  <\f[B]input\f[R] type=\(dqnumber\(dq id=\(dqcaret\-position\(dq min=\(dq0\(dq max=\(dq7\(dq value=\(dq2\(dq />
</\f[B]label\f[R]>
<\f[B]button\f[R]>Move caret</\f[B]button\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] input = document.getElementById(\(dqcaret\-box\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] position = document.getElementById(\(dqcaret\-position\(dq);

document.querySelector(\(dqbutton\(dq).addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] index = position.valueAsNumber;
  input.focus();
  input.setSelectionRange(index, index);
});
.EE
.SS Result
